\begin{equation*}
\int_{[0,1]^{\mathcal{F} \sigma}} x(F) \mathbf{P}_{F_{n}}^{\sigma, \eta}(d x)=\mathbf{E}[p(F,(M, \boldsymbol{\theta}))] \tag{18}
\end{equation*}


where $F=(M, \theta)$ and $\boldsymbol{\theta}$ is constructed as in Definition 9.

On the other hand, $p^{F_{n}}\left(\llbracket F \rrbracket_{\sigma, \eta}\right)$ is the probability that a random injective mapping $[k] \longrightarrow M$ consistent with $\theta$ on $\operatorname{im}(\eta)$ defines a model embedding and the resulting $\sigma$-flag is\\
